-- title:
--   Weighted Embedded Average Le Full Average
-- statement:
--   **Weighted embedded direction average is bounded by the full direction average.** Let $f$ be a nonnegative error-valued function on the successor coordinate directions. Let $E$ denote the embedding of predecessor directions into successor directions, and let $W$ denote the transverse-direction weight. Then
--
--   $$
--   W\,\mathbb E_{i\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathrm{Fin}(m))} f(E(i))
--   \le
--   \mathbb E_{j\sim\operatorname{Unif}(\mathrm{Fin}(m+1))} f(j).
--   $$
--
--   Here $W=m/(m+1)$, and $f(i)\ge0$ for every successor direction. The left side is the normalized sum over the embedded directions, while the right side includes the additional successor direction and all terms are nonnegative. This is the common averaging step for the weighted axis-parallel, weighted diagonal, and answer-valued diagonal bounds.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.MainInductionStep.weighted_embedded_average_le_full_average`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
